# mgoffice.msg - the door of Moriarty's office (mgoffice.ssl). One entry per line; no braces in comments.

# 100 to 102: look (locked, unlocked) and examine.
{100}{}{You see a heavy door with a heavier lock.}
{101}{}{You see a heavy door. Its lock hangs open.}
{102}{}{The door to Moriarty's office. The lock is the one thing in the saloon he paid full price for.}

# 110 to 113: the key.
{110}{}{It is locked. Somebody in this saloon keeps the key close.}
{111}{}{Moriarty's key turns in the lock.}
{112}{}{You turn the key. The door is locked again.}
{113}{}{Close the door before you lock it.}

# 120 to 124: the lock picked, or not.
{120}{}{The lock gives, with a click that sounds very loud to you.}
{121}{}{The lock is better than you are, this time.}
{122}{}{Your pick slips and rings against the plate. You hold your breath. Nobody comes.}
{123}{}{It is not locked.}
{124}{}{There is nothing electronic about this lock. It is iron, spite and a spring.}

{130}{}{You find no traps. Moriarty trusts his lock.}
